# Review Notes

## Summary
T063: `oal probe` replays a batch's recorded safe requests against a
live base URL and diffs status codes and response shapes against the
contract. Findings carry class spec_friction and origin server in a new
conformance.v1 document; friction.v1 stays participant-oriented.

## Design decisions
- Allowlist: an exchange replays only when the operator named its
  operation AND its method is GET, HEAD, or OPTIONS (writes require
  --allow-writes). Skips are recorded with reasons; redirects are
  manual so a 3xx compares as a status and never re-issues a write.
- Vocabulary: conformance.v1 is a new schema. friction.v1's origin enum
  (api/harness/external) describes participant incidents; server
  divergence is not one. The task text said "origin server"; the
  document records exactly that.
- Credential: read from the env var named by --credential-env. The
  value feeds the outgoing header and the Redactor secrets registry,
  nothing else. Header-location schemes only: an apiKey in a query or
  cookie is refused with exit 4 before any request, because the
  document records header names only and an unauthenticated replay
  would blame the server for the probe's own 401.
- Write replay sends the recorded redacted body; documented as such.

## Review round
First implementation drew fix_first from both reviewers over one
blocker class: the writer could emit documents violating conformance.v1
caps on ordinary traffic (600 findings vs 512; 40-header responses;
50-violation bodies; 20001 result rows; over-long detail strings).
Fixed in 049008b before landing:
- Every schema bound is honored at the writer (DOCUMENT_BOUNDS); true
  totals stay in counts; extensions.truncation lists every clip; a
  warning diagnostic reports it. A clipped document never understates
  the divergence.
- The assembled document is validated against conformance.v1 before
  the write-once directory is created; invalid documents are refused
  (exit 3) and nothing is written.
- base_url stores the normalized URL; unparseable JSON with a JSON
  media type is a body_malformed violation, never a conformant string;
  an allowlist longer than the document records is refused up front.

## Verdict
Approved after fix round — landed as 81cc727 + 049008b.
